    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0077" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114 Sick/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-10T22:00:00+01:00">August 10, 1943—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 11—2:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2504. Subject matter Department’s 861, August 6, 8 p.m., and 862, August 6, 9
                        p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d43-f1"/> has been taken up with Foreign Office.
                    Secretary General informed me today that he has authorization from Prime
                    Minister to say that Swedish Government not only has no objection to use of port
                    of Goteborg for purposes planned but will be glad to be of any possible
                    assistance in effecting exchange of wounded war prisoners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
